84. Power to make rules regarding notices of and inquiries into accidents. The Authority may make rules 2consistent with this Act the ordinance and any other enactment for the time being in force for all or any of the following purposes, namely: —

(a) for prescribing the forms of the notices mentioned in the last foregoing section, and the particulars of the accident which those notices are to contain;

(b) for prescribing the class of accidents of which notice is to be sent by telegraph immediately after the accident has occurred ;

(c) for prescribing the duties of railway servants, police officers, the Authority and Magistrates on the occurrence of an accident.
